  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 5,
  "reason": "The claim that 'each of the 26 cantons is allocated one vote, regardless of its population size' directly contradicts the reference, which specifies that six half-cantons (Obwalden, Nidwalden, Basel-Stadt, Basel-Landschaft, Appenzell Ausserrhoden, and Appenzell Innerrhoden) each have half a cantonal vote, while the other 20 cantons have one full vote. This misrepresentation of the cantonal voting system constitutes a factual error.",
  "evidence": "In Swiss referendums, each of the 26 cantons is allocated one vote, regardless of its population size."
}
